ousehold. This is violated by having a larger compumpion than just R+, but rather X_i \u2286 R^L \u00d7 R^L(I-1) \u00d7 R^J (i.e. household also cares about the consumption bundles of all other households, and also cares about the production plans of all firms). However, markets only exist for the L commodities that the consumer buys, so it takes the decisions of other agents as given."]}, "id": "BB_2", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.3, "y": 56.1, "width": 71.6, "height": 17.2, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_3", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.3, "y": 56.1, "width": 71.6, "height": 17.2, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_3", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 14.3, "y": 56.1, "width": 71.6, "height": 17.2, "rotation": 0, "text": ["In the example, the way to solve the problem is to let consumers sell pollution permits. In particular, we think of the consumer as having an endowment of permits, and selling them to firms. However, we can rewrite the budget constraint 12 as"]}, "id": "BB_3", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 37.6, "y": 73.3, "width": 24.4, "height": 5.3, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_4", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 37.6, "y": 73.3, "width": 24.4, "height": 5.3, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["equation"]}, "id": "BB_4", "from_name": "label", "to_